sn35.229:3.4 | S: with its saltwater crocodiles and monsters, <j>its waves and dangers. | T: With its dangers of sharks, demons, waves.
sn35.229:4.1 | S: They’ve slipped their chains, given up death, and have no attachments. | T: “The tie-surmounter, death-forsaker, without acquisitions,
sn35.229:4.2 | S: They’ve given up suffering, <j>so there are no more future lives. | T: Has abandoned suffering for no renewed existence.
sn35.229:4.3 | S: They’ve disappeared, and cannot be measured; | T: Passed away, he cannot be measured,
sn35.229:4.4 | S: and they’ve confounded the King of Death, I say.” | T: I say: He has bewildered the King of Death.”

